      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who owns Precor?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Peloton. It completed its $420 million purchase of Precor from the Amer Sports group on 1 April 2021. Peloton explored selling Precor but decided not to, and in 2025 combined it with its business-to-business arm into a Commercial Business Unit. Peloton's fiscal 2026 results, published in August 2026, still report Precor-brand equipment sales.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Precor still make home treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not that we could find on 20 October 2026. Precor's home store listed strength equipment, bikes and a stretch trainer but no treadmill, and its old Energy and Precision Series home models showed as unavailable at the retailers we checked. Precor's current treadmills, the TRM 800, 700, 600 and 500 lines, are commercial, though dealers can sell them for home use.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do Precor treadmills need a 20-amp outlet?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The current TRM 800, 700 and 600 lines do. Precor specifies a 120-volt, 20-amp individual branch circuit with a NEMA 5-20R receptacle in the US. Precor's figures for the TRM 500 conflict between 15 and 20 amps. Older models vary, so check the label and manual, and never use an extension cord.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is a used Precor treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on model, console and condition. On 20 October 2026 one US remanufacturer listed TRM 885 treadmills at $4,099 and $4,899 and a TRM 781 at $4,699, each with a one-year parts and on-site labour warranty. Private and gym-liquidation sales are much cheaper but usually come with no warranty or delivery. Prices change often.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the Precor warranty transfer to a second owner?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. Precor's warranty for commercial treadmills sold into a home covers the original purchaser only and says it cannot be assigned or resold. It gives a lifetime frame, ten years on parts, three on the console and one year of labour. A used Precor relies on whatever written warranty the reseller provides.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the difference between the Precor TRM 885 and TRM 835?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "They are the same TRM 800-line base with different consoles. The TRM 885 has the 16-inch P84 touchscreen and the TRM 835 the P31 LED console; both have a 4 HP AC motor, 0.5 to 16 mph, minus 3 to 15% incline and a 400 lb rating, according to Precor. Older TRM 885 and 835 units with P80, P82 or P30 consoles are earlier generations.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-10-20",
      dateModified: "2026-10-20",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
};
